   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Universal correlative structure",
     "texto": [
      "The clause is divided into two sentences:"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Element",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Case and function",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Syntactic position",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Example",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
      [
       {
        "texto": "Clause with wer",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Case according to its own clause (wer/wen/wem)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Subordinate clause (verb at the end)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Wer regelmäßig Sport treibt, …",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ],
      [
       {
        "texto": "Clause with der",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Case according to the main clause (der/den/dem)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "Main clause (inversion: der + verb)",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       {
        "texto": "… der bleibt im Alter fit.",
        "lengua": "estudio"
       }
      ]
     ],
     "nota": "",
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Independent functional agreement",
     "texto": [
      "The pronoun «wer» (nominative), «wen» (accusative) or «wem» (dative) is governed by its own subordinate clause. The main clause picks up that person with «der» (nominative), «den» (accusative) or «dem» (dative), according to the syntactic function it performs in the main clause. For example: **Wer fleißig lernt, der besteht die Prüfung** (nominative in both clauses); **Wem das Team vertraut, den wählt man zum Sprecher** («wem» is dative because of «vertrauen»; «den» is accusative because of «wählen»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
